IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lt-common`
IMPORT `rcr-core`

-- Cases for rcr-core.l4: the Local Government (Rates and Charges Remissions) Act 1991 and Regulations 2024 (Tas).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts. The reg 5 indexation was checked in an independent
-- calculator written from the words of reg 5 (scratchpad au-tas-4/hand.py), with exact fractions; no value was copied
-- from the encoding's output. The Hobart CPI figures below are ILLUSTRATIVE (137.1 for March 2024, 139.3 for March 2025,
-- 142.0 for March 2026, 145.5 for March 2027): the ABS figures are not deposited. Regulative rules: asserted with
-- EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line otherwise. Clock: days.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- Rates and Charges Remissions Act 1991 core`

§§ `reg 4 -- eligible pensioner`

`no card or pension` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`an aged pensioner with a concession card` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS TRUE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`a pensioner travelling overseas` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS TRUE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`a health care card holder` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS TRUE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`an MRCA s 199 veteran` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS TRUE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`a VEA war widow` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS TRUE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS FALSE

`an MRCA war widower` MEANS `Cards and pensions` WITH
    `holds a current pensioner concession card in operation` IS FALSE
    `holds a current pensioner concession card inoperative only because temporarily out of Australia` IS FALSE
    `holds a current health care card` IS FALSE
    `is a person to whom VEA s 24 or MRCA s 199 applies` IS FALSE
    `receives a war widow's or widower's pension under VEA Part II or IV at the s 30(1) rate` IS FALSE
    `was the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member to whom MRCA s 12 applies` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `no card or pension`)
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `an aged pensioner with a concession card`
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `a pensioner travelling overseas`
-- A Health Care Card is enough for the rates remission (it is not for the land tax exemption, finding 2).
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `a health care card holder`
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `an MRCA s 199 veteran`
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `a VEA war widow`
#ASSERT `is an eligible pensioner under reg 4` `an MRCA war widower`

§§ `s 4(3)-(3C) and reg 6 -- occupying the property`

`living at home` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in the property, as their principal dwelling`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS FALSE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`single, in aged care, first year` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`single, in aged care, second year` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 1

`single, in aged care, third year` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 2

`single, in aged care, house let` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS TRUE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`single, in aged care, no declaration` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS FALSE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`married, in a nursing-home type hospital bed, spouse at home, fourth year` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a hospital as a nursing-home type patient under the Health Insurance Act 1973 s 3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS TRUE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `in the property, as their principal dwelling`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS FALSE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 3

`married, both in a psychiatric care facility` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a facility providing residential psychiatric or psychological care`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS TRUE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `in a facility providing residential psychiatric or psychological care`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`married, in aged care, spouse living with their daughter` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS TRUE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

`single, living with their daughter` MEANS `Occupation on 1 July` WITH
    `where the person lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `is married or in a significant relationship` IS FALSE
    `where the spouse lives` IS `somewhere else`
    `the person or the spouse received rental income from the property` IS FALSE
    `a statutory declaration under s 4(3A) or (3B) has been provided` IS TRUE
    `consecutive financial years just before this one remitted while in an institution under s 4(3)(a) or (b)(i)` IS 0

#ASSERT `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `living at home`
#ASSERT `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, in aged care, first year`
#ASSERT `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, in aged care, second year`
-- s 4(3C): not more than 2 consecutive financial years (finding 17).
#ASSERT NOT (`is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, in aged care, third year`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, in aged care, house let`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, in aged care, no declaration`)
-- s 4(3)(b)(ii): the spouse at home; s 4(3C) does not reach it, so a fourth year counts.
#ASSERT `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `married, in a nursing-home type hospital bed, spouse at home, fourth year`
#ASSERT `is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `married, both in a psychiatric care facility`
#ASSERT NOT (`is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `married, in aged care, spouse living with their daughter`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is occupying the property as a principal dwelling under s 4` `single, living with their daughter`)
#ASSERT `is in a prescribed institution under reg 6` `in a residential care facility under the Aged Care Act 1997 s 41-3`
#ASSERT NOT (`is in a prescribed institution under reg 6` `somewhere else`)

§§ `s 4(1)-(1D) -- applying, granting, the years remitted`

-- "before 31 March": the last day in 2026-27 is 30 March 2027 (finding 14).
#ASSERT `the last day to apply in the financial year` 2026 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 30
#ASSERT `the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` (YearMonthDay 2027 3 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30))
#ASSERT `the application is made before 31 March in its financial year` (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1)
#ASSERT `the financial year of` (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) EQUALS 2027
#ASSERT `the financial year of` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30) EQUALS 2026

`applied 10 August 2026` MEANS `Application` WITH
    `the day of application` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10
    `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying` IS TRUE
    `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality` IS TRUE

`applied 15 April 2027` MEANS `Application` WITH
    `the day of application` IS YearMonthDay 2027 4 15
    `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying` IS TRUE
    `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality` IS TRUE

`applied 1 July 2027` MEANS `Application` WITH
    `the day of application` IS YearMonthDay 2027 7 1
    `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying` IS TRUE
    `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality` IS TRUE

`applied by a tenant who pays no rates` MEANS `Application` WITH
    `the day of application` IS YearMonthDay 2026 8 10
    `the applicant is an eligible pensioner when applying` IS TRUE
    `the applicant is liable to pay rates or charges to the municipality` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `is an application under s 4(1)` `applied 10 August 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an application under s 4(1)` `applied 15 April 2027`)
#ASSERT `is an application under s 4(1)` `applied 1 July 2027`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an application under s 4(1)` `applied by a tenant who pays no rates`)

#ASSERT `the municipality is to grant the application under s 4(1A)` `applied 10 August 2026` TRUE TRUE
-- Became a pensioner on 2 July 2026: not an eligible pensioner on 1 July 2026, so not granted for 2026-27.
#ASSERT NOT (`the municipality is to grant the application under s 4(1A)` `applied 10 August 2026` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the municipality is to grant the application under s 4(1A)` `applied 10 August 2026` TRUE FALSE)

`granted in 2026, eligible throughout` MEANS `Remission history` WITH
    `the application` IS `applied 10 August 2026`
    `the application was granted under s 4(1A)` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about` IS TRUE

`granted in 2026, moved out before 1 July 2028` MEANS `Remission history` WITH
    `the application` IS `applied 10 August 2026`
    `the application was granted under s 4(1A)` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application` IS FALSE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about` IS FALSE

-- Not granted for 2026-27 (moved out before 1 July 2026, still liable for the rates), but eligible and living there on
-- 1 July 2025: s 4(1D) still remits 2025-26 (finding 16).
`refused for 2026, eligible in 2025` MEANS `Remission history` WITH
    `the application` IS `applied 10 August 2026`
    `the application was granted under s 4(1A)` IS FALSE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about` IS FALSE

-- Applied late, on 1 July 2027 (2027-28), having been eligible since 1 July 2026: s 4(1D) brings back 2026-27.
`applied on 1 July 2027, eligible in 2026` MEANS `Remission history` WITH
    `the application` IS `applied 1 July 2027`
    `the application was granted under s 4(1A)` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on 1 July of the year before the application` IS TRUE
    `eligible pensioner and occupying on every 1 July after the year of the application, up to the year asked about` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, eligible throughout` 2026
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, eligible throughout` 2025
#ASSERT NOT (`the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, eligible throughout` 2024)
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, eligible throughout` 2029
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, moved out before 1 July 2028` 2026
#ASSERT NOT (`the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, moved out before 1 July 2028` 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `granted in 2026, moved out before 1 July 2028` 2028)
#ASSERT NOT (`the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `refused for 2026, eligible in 2025` 2026)
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `refused for 2026, eligible in 2025` 2025
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `applied on 1 July 2027, eligible in 2026` 2026
#ASSERT `the financial year is remitted under s 4(1B)-(1D)` `applied on 1 July 2027, eligible in 2026` 2027

§§ `s 4(2) and reg 5 -- the maximum`

`the illustrative CPI figures` MEANS LIST 137.1, 139.3, 142.0, 145.5

-- A Hobart CPI fall in March 2026, then a rise.
`the illustrative CPI figures with a fall` MEANS LIST 137.1, 139.3, 138.5, 141.0

-- No change in the Hobart CPI from March 2024 to March 2025.
`flat CPI figures` MEANS LIST 137.1, 137.1

#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest cent under reg 5(5)` 385.495 EQUALS 385.50
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest cent under reg 5(5)` 385.4949 EQUALS 385.49
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest dollar under reg 5(6)` 385.50 EQUALS 386
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest dollar under reg 5(6)` 385.49 EQUALS 385

-- 2024-25: the reg 5(4) base.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2024 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 379.41
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2024 FALSE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 558.50
-- 2025-26, water and sewerage customer: 379.41 x 139.3 / 137.1 = 385.4983 -> 385.50 (to the cent) -> $386 (to the dollar).
-- Rounding straight to the dollar would give $385 (finding 11).
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2025 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 386
-- 2026-27: 385.4983 (B, before rounding) x 142.0 / 139.3 = 392.9702 -> $393.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2026 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 393
-- 2027-28: 392.9702 x 145.5 / 142.0 = 402.6561 -> $403.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2027 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 403
-- Not a customer: 558.50 x 139.3 / 137.1 = 567.4621 -> $567; x 142.0 / 139.3 = 578.4610 -> $578; x 145.5 / 142.0 = 592.7188 -> $593.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2025 FALSE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 567
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2026 FALSE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 578
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2027 FALSE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 593
-- reg 5(3): the CPI falls to 138.5 in March 2026: 385.4983 x 138.5 / 139.3 = 383.2844 -> $383, less than $386, so 2026-27
-- stays $386. 2027-28: B stays 385.4983 (finding 12): x 141.0 / 138.5 = 392.4567 -> $392. (Carrying 383.2844 instead
-- would give $390.)
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2026 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures with a fall` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 386
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2027 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures with a fall` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 392
-- No CPI change: 379.41 x 1 = 379.41 -> $379, less than $379.41, so 2025-26 stays $379.41.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2025 TRUE `flat CPI figures` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 379.41
-- Not covered: before 2024-25, or a CPI figure missing.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2023 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `not covered` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2024: the maximum remission for it is set by regulations that are not deposited (the 2024 Regulations start from 2024-25)`
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2028 TRUE `the illustrative CPI figures` EQUALS `not covered` `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2024 TRUE (LIST 137.1) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 379.41
-- reg 5(4) sets 2024-25 directly, so it needs no CPI figure; 2025-26 needs March 2024 (D) and March 2025 (C); 2027-28
-- needs the four from March 2024 to March 2027 (finding 23).
#ASSERT `the number of Hobart CPI figures reg 5 needs for` 2024 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the number of Hobart CPI figures reg 5 needs for` 2025 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of Hobart CPI figures reg 5 needs for` 2027 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2024 TRUE EMPTY EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 379.41
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2024 FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 558.50
-- 2025-26 with March 2024 alone: C (March 2025) is missing.
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2025 TRUE (LIST 137.1) EQUALS `not covered` `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum remission for` 2027 TRUE (LIST 137.1, 139.3, 142.0) EQUALS `not covered` `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`

-- The amount: 30% of $1 800 = $540, capped at $393; 30% of $1 000 = $300, under the cap.
#ASSERT `the amount remitted under s 4(1B) and (2)` 1800 393 EQUALS 393
#ASSERT `the amount remitted under s 4(1B) and (2)` 1000 393 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the amount remitted under s 4(1B) and (2)` 1310 393 EQUALS 393

§§ `s 4(4)-(8) -- the surviving spouse`

#ASSERT `the surviving spouse may apply under s 4(4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the surviving spouse may apply under s 4(4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the surviving spouse may apply under s 4(4)` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a surviving spouse's application can cover the year under s 4(6)` 2026 2026 FALSE
#ASSERT `a surviving spouse's application can cover the year under s 4(6)` 2026 2025 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a surviving spouse's application can cover the year under s 4(6)` 2026 2025 FALSE)
-- s 4(6): never a later year.
#ASSERT NOT (`a surviving spouse's application can cover the year under s 4(6)` 2026 2027 TRUE)

-- s 4(7): applied in 2026-27 and died in 2026-27: 2026-27 and 2025-26 go to the spouse.
#ASSERT `the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2026 2026 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2026 2025 TRUE TRUE
-- s 4(8): applied in 2026-27, died in 2028-29: only 2028-29; nothing for 2029-30.
#ASSERT `the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2028 2028 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2028 2029 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2028 2027 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the surviving spouse is to be given the unpaid remission under s 4(7)-(8)` 2026 2028 2028 TRUE FALSE)

§§ `ss 4(9), 4A, 4B-4F -- notices, penalties, review`

#ASSERT `the last day to notify the municipality under s 4(9)` 2026 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 30
#ASSERT `the most penalty units for an offence against s 4(9)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the most penalty units for an offence against s 4A` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the days to object under s 4C` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the days to apply for review under s 4F` EQUALS 60

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- s 4(1), (1A): clock starts on 1 July 2026; the last day, 30 March 2027, is day 272.
#ASSERT `days from` (`1 July of` 2026) `to` (`the last day to apply in the financial year` 2026) EQUALS 272
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` 272 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the municipality for the remission` 40), (EVENT `the municipality` `remit 30% of the rates and charges, up to the prescribed maximum` 70)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` 272 TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 273)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` 272 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the municipality for the remission` 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An application on day 273 (31 March 2027) comes too late: nothing is owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` 272 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the municipality for the remission` 273)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the municipality's obligation to remit 30% of the rates and charges, up to the prescribed maximum, still pending (applied on day 272, 30 March 2027)
#TRACE `s 4(1), (1A) -- the eligible pensioner may apply before 31 March, and the municipality is to grant the remission` 272 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply to the municipality for the remission` AT 272

-- s 4(9): ceased on 15 November 2026 (day 0); the end of the year, 30 June 2027, is day 227.
#ASSERT `days from` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 15) `to` (`the last day to notify the municipality under s 4(9)` 2026) EQUALS 227
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(9) -- the person given the remission must notify the municipality before the end of the year` TRUE 227) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person given the remission` `notify the municipality in writing` 227)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4(9) -- the person given the remission must notify the municipality before the end of the year` FALSE 227) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 300)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person given the remission, "s 4(9): a person given a remission must notify ..." (notice on day 228, 1 July 2027)
#TRACE `s 4(9) -- the person given the remission must notify the municipality before the end of the year` TRUE 227 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person given the remission` DOES `notify the municipality in writing` AT 228

-- s 4A: information given over 10 days.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4A -- the applicant must not make a false or misleading statement` 10) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 11)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 4A: a person must not, in giving information ..." (a false statement on day 3)
#TRACE `s 4A -- the applicant must not make a false or misleading statement` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `make a statement known to be false or misleading` AT 3

-- s 4B.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4B -- the person given the remission must repay it when the Commissioner requires` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person given the remission` `repay the amount remitted` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 4B -- the person given the remission must repay it when the Commissioner requires` FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the obligation to repay the amount remitted, still pending (no period is set, so time alone never breaches it)
#TRACE `s 4B -- the person given the remission must repay it when the Commissioner requires` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- ss 4C, 4E, 4F: objection on day 60, determination on day 90, review applied for on day 150 (60 days after).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 4C, 4E, 4F -- the person may object within 60 days, and then apply for review within 60 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person given the remission` `lodge a written objection with the Commissioner` 60), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `determine the objection and give written notice` 90), (EVENT `the objector` `apply to the Magistrates Court for a review` 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 4C, 4E, 4F -- the person may object within 60 days, and then apply for review within 60 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person given the remission` `lodge a written objection with the Commissioner` 60), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `determine the objection and give written notice` 90), (WAITUNTIL 151)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 4C, 4E, 4F -- the person may object within 60 days, and then apply for review within 60 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 61)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Commissioner's obligation to determine the objection and give written notice, still pending (objection on day 30)
#TRACE `ss 4C, 4E, 4F -- the person may object within 60 days, and then apply for review within 60 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person given the remission` DOES `lodge a written objection with the Commissioner` AT 30
